# Original upload bundle (redundant — contents live in files/)
files.zip

# Secrets (HANDOFF §8: never commit)
.env

# Fetched odds cache (a runtime artifact, not source — ODDS-07). Its ABSENCE is the normal
# first-run state and is handled fail-soft (rating-only + banner). scripts/fetch_odds.py writes
# it; the app only ever READS it via ui/odds_loader.py.
data/odds_cache.json

# Fetched live-results cache (a runtime artifact, not source — RES-01). Its ABSENCE is the normal
# first-run state and is handled fail-soft (manual entry + banner). scripts/fetch_results.py writes
# it; the app only ever READS it via ui/results_loader.py. (data/team_aliases.json + data/stageN.json
# are NOT ignored — those are committed source.)
data/results_cache.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.uv/
.pytest_cache/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.gstack/

# Scratch / throwaway artifacts (probe scripts, ad-hoc number dumps, screenshot crops).
# The leading underscore is the project's "disposable" convention. Real screenshots live in
# docs/assets/ (no underscore prefix), so they are NOT ignored.
scripts/_*.py
_*.png
_*.md

# Internal planning / spec / agent docs — kept LOCAL, not published. The public doc surface is
# README.md + ROADMAP.md + STATUS.md + docs/. These hold the detailed GSD process trail and the
# original spec, useful while building but noise (and half-baked thinking) for a public audience.
.planning/
files/
CLAUDE.md
